{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e274fa5f-fc9a-44f2-b314-320a9e38f535",
    "name": "Mekari eSign Open API v1 - Public",
    "description": "eSign Open API provides an application interface that allows your application to perform eSignatures as well as eMeterai stamps.\n\n# Prerequisites\n\nTo be able to use the API you are required to get `client_id` and `client_secret` to perform the authentication flows.\n\n- For OAuth2 flow, please contact our team to obtain the client credentials\n    \n- For HMAC flow, please create on [[Sandbox] Mekari Developer Center (MDC) ](https://sandbox-developers.mekari.com/docs/kb) directly\n    \n\n# Environments\n\nBelow are environments that can be used for development as well as for production purposes.\n\n## eSign Open API\n\n| **Environment** | **eSign Base URL (OAuth2)** | **eSign Base URL (HMAC)** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Production | [https://api.mekari.com/v2/esign/v1](https://api.mekari.com/v2/esign/v1) | [https://api.mekari.com/v2/esign-hmac/v1](https://api.mekari.com/v2/esign-hmac/v1) |\n| Sandbox | [https://sandbox-api.mekari.com/v2/esign/v1](https://sandbox-api.mekari.com/v2/esign/v1) | [https://sandbox-api.mekari.com/v2/esign-hmac/v1](https://sandbox-api.mekari.com/v2/esign-hmac/v1) |\n| Staging _(need VPN)_ | [https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign/v1](https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign/v1) | [https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign-hmac/v1](https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign-hmac/v1) |\n| Playground _(need VPN)_ | [https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign-playground/v1](https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign-playground/v1) | [https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign-playground-hmac/v1](https://api.mekari.io/v2/esign-playground-hmac/v1) |\n| Mock Server | [https://58fdbadf-ae2d-4965-b892-10aa4ca64ebd.mock.pstmn.io](https://58fdbadf-ae2d-4965-b892-10aa4ca64ebd.mock.pstmn.io) | N/A |\n\n## Mekari SSO\n\n| **Environment** | **SSO Auth Base URL** | **SSO Base URL** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Production | [https://account.mekari.com](https://account.mekari.com) | [https://api.mekari.com](https://api.mekari.com) |\n| Sandbox | [https://sandbox-account.mekari.com](https://sandbox-account.mekari.com) | [https://sandbox-api.mekari.com](https://sandbox-api.mekari.com) |\n| Staging _(need VPN)_ | [https://account.mekari.io](https://account.mekari.io) | [https://api.mekari.com](https://api.mekari.com) |\n| Mock Server | [https://sandbox-account.mekari.com](https://sandbox-account.mekari.com) | [https://sandbox-api.mekari.com](https://sandbox-api.mekari.com) |\n\n## Mekari Developer Center\n\n| **Environment** | **MDC URL** |\n| --- | --- |\n| Production | [https://developers.mekari.com](https://developers.mekari.com) |\n| Sandbox | [https://sandbox-developers.mekari.com](https://sandbox-developers.mekari.com) |\n| Staging _(Need VPN)_ | [https://developers.mekari.io](https://developers.mekari.io) |\n\n# Authentication\n\neSign Open API provides 2 authentication flows that serve different purposes and use cases.\n\n- OAuth2, for client-to-server integration and client integrator use cases.\n    \n- HMAC, server-to-server integration suitable for non-client integrator use cases.\n    \n\nFor further suggestions that are suitable to use case needs, please contact our team.\n\n## OAuth2\n\n1. Get `authorize_code`\n    \n\n| URL |\n| --- |\n| {{sso_auth_base_url}}/auth?client_id={client_id}&response_type=code&scope=esign |\n\nReplace `sso_base_url` and `client_id` with the target environment variable. It will be redirected to callback_url with code.\n\n2\\. Get access token using obtained `authorize_code`\n\n``` bash\ncurl --location '{{sso_base_url}}/oauth2/token' \\\n--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n--data '{\n    \"client_id\": \"{{client_id}}\",\n    \"client_secret\": \"{{client_secret}}\",\n    \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\",\n    \"code\": \"{{authorization_code}}\"\n}'\n\n ```\n\n3\\. Use the access token to access eSign endpoint\n\n``` bash\ncurl --location '{{base_url}}/profile' \\\n--header 'Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}'\n\n ```\n\n## HMAC\n\nUse the generated HMAC signature combined with the following format of headers to access the eSign endpoint\n\n``` bash\ncurl --request GET 'https://sandbox-api.mekari.com/v2/esign-hmac/v1/profile' \\\n        --header 'Authorization: hmac username=\"{{client_id}}\", algorithm=\"hmac-sha256\", headers=\"date request-line\", signature=\"zvVJc1v/tsTKiSVgTN7eGTXwbmjPV7AB8mPnrMnQxjU=\"' \\\n        --header 'Date: Tue, 26 Mar 2024 05:15:58 GMT' \\\n        --header 'Content-Type: application/json'\n\n ```\n\nFor detail of HMAC authentication flow follow [HMAC Authentication](https://sandbox-developers.mekari.com/docs/kb/hmac-authentication)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
